Can't run PineScript-style indicators in our charting tool

Our charting tool uses `oakscriptjs` to calculate indicators and display them over bar data. I need the script API and its supporting calculations, session handling, symbol requests, and drawing outputs working together so users can reuse their PineScript indicator logic. For example, with our loaded bars:

```typescript
import { executeScript, indicator, plot, ta, close } from 'oakscriptjs/script';
const run = executeScript(() => {
  indicator('Smoothed price', { overlay: true });
  plot(ta.sma(close, 8), 'Average close');
}, bars);
const plots = run.result.plots;
```

This should return the indicator's declarations and plotted data as documented. Instead, execution throws `not implemented`.

The unfinished code is in these package files:

- `src/script/index.ts`, `src/runtime/series.ts`, `src/ta-series.ts`;
- `src/compare/index.ts`, `src/math/index.ts`, `src/ta/index.ts`, `src/ta/limits.ts`, `src/utils/index.ts`;
- `src/security/other.ts`, `src/security/resample.ts`, `src/session/bars.ts`, `src/session/calendar.ts`, `src/session/context.ts`;
- `src/time/index.ts`, `src/time/session.ts`, `src/time/timezone.ts`, `src/timeframe/index.ts`;
- `src/drawing/bar-time.ts`, `src/drawing/output.ts`, `src/drawing/registry.ts`, `src/table/index.ts`.

